00:13:06,600 --> 00:13:10,000
anticoagulation concern,
malignancy, recent

245
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:12,280
surgery over the
area, and aneurysm.

246
00:13:12,400 --> 00:13:15,840
The broader lesson is
that myofascial release is

247
00:13:15,840 --> 00:13:18,960
generally gentle, but gentle
does not mean appropriate

248
00:13:18,960 --> 00:13:22,560
for everyone. So make sure
you have, you make sure

249
00:13:22,560 --> 00:13:25,620
that it is still clinically
relevant and appropriate.

250
00:13:26,260 --> 00:13:29,520
So the last major technique
that we'll be discussing

251
00:13:29,520 --> 00:13:33,460
is BLT, balanced ligamous
tension. The central

252
00:13:33,460 --> 00:13:36,980
concept is that ligament
around an articulation exists

253
00:13:36,980 --> 00:13:40,420
under reciprocal tension.
With somatic dysfunction,

254
00:13:40,760 --> 00:13:44,260
those forces are no longer
balanced normally. Rather

255
00:13:44,260 --> 00:13:48,040
than forcing the joint through
the barrier, BLT seeks a

256
00:13:48,040 --> 00:13:51,520
position in which abnormal
ligament's tension is

257
00:13:51,520 --> 00:13:55,700
minimized and balanced. This
is why BLT is often a very

258
00:13:55,700 --> 00:13:59,860
useful option when we want a
comparatively gentle approach,

259
00:13:59,860 --> 00:14:04,360
especially in inpatient
setting. For the RIS, we're

260
00:14:04,360 --> 00:14:06,760
considering the caustral
vertebral and caustral

261
00:14:06,760 --> 00:14:10,400
transverse relationship as
part of the dysfunctional unit.

262
00:14:11,600 --> 00:14:14,880
So similar to BLT of the
spine, BLT of the ribs

263
00:14:14,880 --> 00:14:17,960
follow a very similar
sequence. For this example,

264
00:14:17,960 --> 00:14:20,200
we're emphasizing
ribs 7 through 10 and

265
00:14:20,200 --> 00:14:22,500
their predominantly
bucket handle component of

266
00:14:22,500 --> 00:14:26,820
motion. So you would
disengage the articulation,

267
00:14:26,940 --> 00:14:31,260
exaggerate the existing
position, or otherwise move

268
00:14:31,260 --> 00:14:33,460
toward a point of balance
depending upon your

269
00:14:33,460 --> 00:14:36,600
approach. It could be direct
or indirect. Most of the

270
00:14:36,600 --> 00:14:39,180
time, it's going to be
exaggerated in the indirect,

271
00:14:39,750 --> 00:14:44,700
and then balance the
tension as you feel it.

272
00:14:44,860 --> 00:14:47,680
Allow the tissue to
respond, and finally

273
00:14:47,680 --> 00:14:52,700
return the rib towards
a neutral and reassess.

274
00:14:52,820 --> 00:14:56,160
The final step is very
important. Every osteopathic

275
00:14:56,160 --> 00:14:58,860
treatment should include
a reassessment. Don't

276
00:14:58,860 --> 00:15:03,200
forget to reassess your
patient and determine whether

277
00:15:03,200 --> 00:15:06,720
you actually made any
changes into this function.

